<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman starts Hermes.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Lehman starts Hermes.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>French luxury goods maker Hermes International was rated &quot;underperform&quot; as Lehman Brothers started coverage of the stock, the investment bank said on Friday.</p>
<p>Analyst John Wakely said the company's earnings growth was slowing and it was in need of greater capital expenditure in its leather business.</p>
<p>Wakely said he expected single-digit earnings growth in 1997 and 1998 and that a slowdown in silk sales would squeeze profits.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
